# Vue 3 Patterns

## Component Structure

Always use `<script setup lang="ts">`:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref, computed, watch } from 'vue'

// Props
const props = defineProps<{ 
  id: number
  data: CardData 
}>()

// State
const isActive = ref(false)

// Computed
const displayName = computed(() => props.data.fullName)

// Methods
function handleClick() {
  isActive.value = true
}
</script>

<template>
  <!-- Single root element for proper event handling -->
  <div class="component-wrapper">
    ...
  </div>
</template>

<style>
/* Component styles */
</style>
```

## State Management

- Use `ref()` for primitives and objects
- Use `reactive()` for complex settings objects
- Use `computed()` for derived state

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const count = ref(0)
const settings = reactive({ value: 1, enabled: true })
const isValid = computed(() => count.value > 0)

// ❌ Avoid - don't mix reactive patterns
const data = reactive({ count: ref(0) })
```

## Event Handling

- Use `@event="handler"` syntax
- For drag events, ensure single root element in template

```vue
<SingleCard 
  @mouseover="preview(card)"
  @dragstart="onDragStart($event, card)"
  draggable="true"
/>
```
